{
  "id": "pgr",
  "term": "PGR",
  "definition": "PGR, or Post-Gaming Return, is a post-game regulatory state in which attention and motivation shift away from gameplay and back to non-gaming activities and goals. It marks temporary disengagement from gaming as an active way of pursuing a goal, rather than directly measuring mood, well-being, problematic gaming, or whether the goal was fully achieved.",
